# Pattern matching for `switch` — guards

## `case` on a type pattern

```java
return switch (obj) {
    case Integer i -> "int " + i;
    case String s  -> "string len " + s.length();
    default        -> "other";
};
```

## `when` guards — add a condition

```java
case String s when s.isBlank() -> "blank";
case String s                  -> "string: " + s;   // more specific FIRST
```

## `null`, and exhaustiveness

```java
case null, default -> "nothing / other";
```

Over a **sealed** type, cover every variant → **no `default`**:

```java
switch (shape) { case Circle c -> …; case Square s -> …; case Triangle t -> …; }
```

Add a variant → won't compile. **Don't** add a `default` "just in case" — it silences that check.
